  "name": "wandering-albatross",
  "notes": "THE ASPECT-RATIO CEILING, and the species that proves `soaring` is not one wing. Hand-wing index separates ocean dynamic soarers from land thermal soarers by a factor of two: an albatross gets its lift from LENGTH and a vulture from AREA, so this bird carries the highest span and the highest aspect ratio in the set and a golden eagle of similar mass carries neither.\n\nAuthored FLYING. Perched it is a white lump; in the air it is a 3 m plank with a body in the middle, and that is the animal.",
